{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790985873,"nonce":"srneQm8dP0yHuPqoUSDLwpFZiGE=","title":"Utility classes: what tw cannot bind yet","message":"ashui.style.Tw generates its classes from the theme's token families. A class with nothing to bind to is a compile error that says why. The gaps:\n\n- **Per-side spacing:** `px-`/`py-`/`pt-`/`pr-`/`pb-`/`pl-`, the `m` forms, `gap-x-`/`gap-y-`. Padding, Margin and Gap are bound as one uniform value. Blinc's layout supports per side; ashui's binding needs a per-side value (one Edges value on Padding/Margin, told apart by variant as CornerShape is).\n- **Relative sizes:** `w-full`, `w-1/2`, `h-screen`, `*-auto`. The size props are px-only Singles; Taffy takes percent and auto.\n- **Letter spacing:** `tracking-*`. The tokens are in ems, so the binding needs the element's font size.\n- **State variants:** `hover:`, `focus:`, `active:`, `disabled:`. They need input events (e532fc0) and a per-element state signal. `dark:` is mostly redundant, since colour classes already follow the scheme.\n- **Transitions:** `duration-*`, `ease-*`. These need a motion system (b2fbc73); the AnimationTokens are already there.\n- **Classes on `\u003ctext\u003e`:** hxx takes `class=` on `\u003cdiv\u003e` only.\n- **Sizes past the spacing scale:** the scale ends at `Space32` (128px), so `w-72`/`w-80` do not exist. Either add tokens or keep attributes for large fixed sizes.","files":null}]}